# ---- Data: never commit. Lives in Databricks Volumes; repo holds loader code only.
#
# THESE RULES FILTER BY FORMAT, WHICH IS NOT THE SAME AS FILTERING BY CONTENT.
# An HTML export of an executed notebook contains cell OUTPUTS -- real names,
# birth dates and salaries from display(people_df.limit(5)) -- and would pass
# every rule below, because it is not a .parquet or a .csv. The policy was about
# data, and the rules were about extensions.
#
# Exports are RELEASE ARTIFACTS, attached to a tagged GitHub Release and archived
# to the audit volume. They are never committed: a snapshot in the tree cannot be
# regenerated from the commit containing it, while a tag records the run that
# produced it.
assignments/**/exports/

data/
*.parquet
*.avro
*.orc
*.csv
*.tsv
*.json.gz
*.zip
*.tar.gz
!docs/**/*.csv

# ---- Spark / Delta local artifacts
spark-warehouse/
metastore_db/
derby.log
_delta_log/
.checkpoint/
*.crc
_SUCCESS

# ---- JetBrains IDE
.idea/
*.iml
out/

# ---- Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
# NO TRAILING SLASH (D.174): a slash matches only a directory, and the snapshot gate links .venv
# to the proven environment, which git records as a symlink.
.venv
venv/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ---- Databricks CLI / auth  (credential leak surface)
.databrickscfg
.databricks/
*.env
.env.*

# ---- Terminal artifacts
#
# A file literally named "...." keeps appearing. It is created by the IntelliJ
# terminal's heredoc handling -- the `>....` continuation prompt -- not by
# anything in this repo, and it has been committed once and staged twice since.
#
# Ignoring it stops `git add -A` from staging it. tests/test_no_data_in_repo.py
# still fails if it is ever force-added, because .gitignore is defeated by
# `git add -f` and by anything already tracked.
....

# ---- macOS
.DS_Store

# Recorded evidence: plan:status and other runs write here.
.artifacts/
